.TH MEMOS-TUI 1 "January 2026" "memento" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
memento \- Terminal user interface for Memos
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B memento
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B memento
is a terminal user interface (TUI) for interacting with a Memos instance.
It allows you to view, create, edit, and delete memos from the command line.
.PP
Memos is a lightweight, self-hosted memo hub. This TUI provides a vim-style
interface for efficient memo management.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug mode. Logs will be written to ~/.local/share/memento/debug.log
.TP
.B \-\-init-config
Create a default configuration file at ~/.config/memento/config.yaml
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.SS List Screen
.TP
.B j / Down
Move down in the list
.TP
.B k / Up
Move up in the list
.TP
.B Enter
View memo details
.TP
.B n
Create new memo
.TP
.B e
Edit selected memo
.TP
.B d
Delete selected memo
.TP
.B p
Toggle pin status
.TP
.B a
Toggle archive status
.TP
.B v
Cycle visibility (Private/Protected/Public)
.TP
.B /
Search memos (fuzzy matching)
.TP
.B r
Refresh memo list
.TP
.B q
Quit
.SS Detail Screen
.TP
.B j / Down
Scroll down
.TP
.B k / Up
Scroll up
.TP
.B e
Edit memo
.TP
.B d
Delete memo
.TP
.B p
Toggle pin status
.TP
.B a
Toggle archive status
.TP
.B v
Cycle visibility
.TP
.B Esc / q
Back to list
.SS Editor (Vim Mode)
.TP
.B i
Enter insert mode
.TP
.B Esc
Return to normal mode
.TP
.B h/j/k/l
Move cursor (left/down/up/right)
.TP
.B w
Move to next word
.TP
.B b
Move to previous word
.TP
.B 0
