.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is read from \fB~/.config/memento/config.yaml\fR.
.PP
Use \fB--init-config\fR to create a default configuration file.
.SS Configuration Options
.TP
.B theme
Color theme: dracula, nord, solarized-dark, solarized-light, gruvbox, one-dark, tokyo-night, catppuccin-mocha, monokai, or custom
.TP
.B date_format
Date display format: relative, short, long, or iso
.TP
.B sort_by
Sort memos by: display_time, create_time, update_time, or pinned_first
.TP
.B sort_order
Sort order: asc or desc
.TP
.B editor.mode
Editor mode: vim or normal
.TP
.B debug
Enable debug logging (true/false)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MEMOS_API_URL
URL of your Memos instance API (e.g., https://memos.example.com/api/v1)
.TP
.B MEMOS_AUTH_TOKEN
Access token for authentication
.PP
These can also be set in a \fB.env\fR file in the current directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/memento/config.yaml
User configuration file
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/memento/debug.log
Debug log file (when debug mode is enabled)
.TP
.B .env
Local environment file for API credentials
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the TUI:
.B memento
.TP
Start with debug logging:
.B memento --debug
.TP
Create default config file:
.B memento --init-config
.SH MOUSE SUPPORT
Mouse support is enabled by default:
.TP
\(bu Click to select a memo in the list
.TP
\(bu Click again on selected memo to open it
.TP
\(bu Scroll wheel to navigate lists
.TP
\(bu Right-click to go back from detail view
